UID:E9qAxaFfLcOWtNqKM6HRH
SUMMARY:The SWAP: Trade Notes. Make Connections
DTSTAMP:20260811T095930Z
DTSTART:20260813T183000Z
DESCRIPTION:Do you have study materials collecting dust? A study strategy t
	hat’s helped you succeed? Are you looking for an accountability partner or
	 extra motivation on your licensure journey? \n\nJoin HNOMA for The Swap\,
	 an interactive event designed to connect aspiring architects\, exam candi
	dates\, and recently licensed professionals. Exchange study materials\, sh
	are test-taking strategies\, and build a supportive community of peers nav
	igating the A.R.E. process.\n\nThe Houston Chapter of NOMA and LeaderFlow 
	are partnering to host this two-part experience. The evening will begin wi
	th a fireside-style panel discussion moderated by LeaderFlow\, featuring p
	rofessionals who will share insights\, lessons learned\, and practical adv
	ice from their licensure journeys. Attendees will then break into smaller 
	groups for facilitated discussions\, providing an opportunity to ask quest
	ions\, exchange resources\, and connect with others at various stages of t
	he A.R.E. process.\n\nWhether you’re exploring licensure for the first tim
	e\, actively studying for exams\, or recently licensed and looking to give
	 back\, we encourage you to join us.\n\nThere’s something valuable for eve
	ryone at The Swap.\n\nPanelists\nShreya Patel\, Harrison Kornberg\nTim Uzo
	igwe\, Perkins & Will\nJaniece Williams\, Leaderflow\nJavier E. Guerrero\,
	 Martinez Architects\nFallon Barrett\, City of Houston\n\nRegister here \n
	\nhttps://architecturehouston.org/event/the-swap-trade-notes-make-connecti
	ons/\n\nFrom AIA Houston
URL:https://architecturehouston.org/event/the-swap-trade-notes-make-connect
	ions/
LOCATION:Perkins & Will\, 1001 McKinney St.\, Houston\, TX\, 77002\, United
	 States
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:aia-houston
CATEGORIES:AIA Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:KtMys9OKxlFNuekgQUcL2
SUMMARY:EP University: Project Delivery
DTSTAMP:20260811T095930Z
DTSTART:20260819T113000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the third session of the EP University Lecture Seri
	es: Project Delivery. \nAll architecture projects have fundamentally follo
	wed the same processes from programming\, to design\, to documentation and
	 construction. This course reveals the step-by-step process in delivering 
	a project from conception to reality. \n\nReview the phases of design – Pr
	ogramming\, Site Planning\, Schematic Design\, and Design Development – to
	 understand the processes and deliverables for each phase\nUnderstand the 
	project team member roles – internal and external – and how projects move 
	from person to person and phase to phase\nUnderstand the process of develo
	ping construction documents to execute the design vision – from cartoon se
	t\, to establishing what to draw\, why to draw it\, and what team members 
	are responsible for confirming constructability and details\nReview the pr
	ocess of formally issuing drawings including sealing documents\, labelling
	 drawings\, permitting documents\, transmitting drawings and handling draw
	ing revisions\n\nPresented by Jeanette Shaw of Powers Brown Architecture\,
	 this session offers 1LU CE credit.  \nLunch is provided. \nLocation: Powe
	rs Brown Architecture\, MKT 600 N Shepherd\, Building 3\, Suite 300\, Hous
	ton\, TX 77007 \nAdvanced registration is required. Deadline: Monday\, Aug
	ust 17 at 5PM.\n\nhttps://architecturehouston.org/event/ep-university-proj
	ect-delivery/\n\nFrom AIA Houston
URL:https://architecturehouston.org/event/ep-university-project-delivery/
LOCATION:Powers Brown Architecture\, MKT 600 N Shepherd\, Building 3\, Suit
	e 300\, Houston\, TX 77007\, 600 N Shepherd\, Building 3\, Ste 300\, Houst
	on\, TX\, 77007
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:aia-houston
CATEGORIES:AIA Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
